### observed TREND exponents, error ~ C Ma^n (measured, not assumed) ###
  over Ma 0.0028802 -> 0.00036003  (a factor of 8)
  drho/rho               n = 1.0178
  relL2(|U|)             n = 0.8848
  relL2(p')              n = 1.0432
  fluxRelDiff            n = 0.9706
  theory for THIS case: the pressure drop is viscous-dominated,
    dp ~ 12 mu U L / H^2, so drho/rho = dp/p ~ Ma^1. A quadratic expectation
    (dp ~ rho U^2) would be wrong here.

